      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T21:40:30Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): an op whose verdict reads the program ahead digests it in its stamp\n\nVerify's prior acquittal (#96) and the turned family's pilot and facing\ncredits (#103) read the setup's earlier ops, but only Pocket3D and Drill\nstamps digested them: a contour acquitted by a face kept reading Ok\nafter the face was regenerated shallower, and a bore kept its pilot's\ncredit after the pilot was deleted - both posted.\n\nEvery op with no 3+2 frame (exactly the set that collects verify's\nprior plan) now writes the existing rest digest into its stamp\n(drill_prior::reads_prior), so editing, regenerating, deleting or\nreordering an earlier op of its setup marks it Stale and the post gate\nrefuses it; stale_reason names the moved predecessor. A posed op keeps\nits stamp bit for bit.\n\nOne-time churn: every non-first unposed op of a saved project reads\nStale once and clears on regenerate. RegenerateAll converges in two\nrounds when a later op reads an earlier one (the M3.1 C law Pocket3D\nalready ran on); the operations suite's batch test now says so.\n\nturning_bore's fixture moved to tests/common/bore.rs to keep the suite\nunder the 400-line law.\n\nPinned by a_face_regenerated_shallower_marks_the_acquitted_contour_stale\n(vertical_rapid_stock) and\na_pilot_deleted_or_made_shallower_after_the_bore_marks_it_stale\n(turning_bore); both fail before the fix.\n\nFixes #109\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
