    "sha": "342bd44ad4d29e1523d941edd6edb8350042ca00",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDM0MmJkNDRhZDRkMjllMTUyM2Q5NDFlZGQ2ZWRiODM1MDA0MmNhMDA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T21:54:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T21:54:59Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): one Regenerate All converges a job whose ops read the program ahead\n\nSince the stamp digests the ops ahead (previous commit), a batch staged\nagainst one frozen world stamped a dependent against its predecessor's\nOLD path: one click left it Stale, a second click cleared it.\n\nRegenerateAll now runs rounds in its constructor: each stages every\nStale op in program order, finishes them on rayon (M5.3 B), and writes\nits results so the next round reads them; it stops when nothing is\nStale, capped at the op count, and names any op still Stale in\n`skipped`. Every write is inverted before construction ends, so apply\nreplays the whole batch as ONE undo unit. `regenerated()` counts\ndistinct ops.\n\nregenerate_all_fixes_the_whole_job_in_one_undo_unit expects one round\nagain; remachining's two-round test now converges in one\n(a_params_edit_converges_in_one_regenerate_all); the threaded-batch\ndeterminism test compares against the ordered apply-as-you-go loop.\nPinned by one_regenerate_all_brings_a_dependent_pair_current\n(vertical_rapid_stock), which fails without this change.\n\nFixes #109\nFixes #145\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
