  {
    "sha": "5cfeaf73aee2f8de3a55d6e0aca2ba49ad764673",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDVjZmVhZjczYWVlMmY4ZGUzYTU1ZDZlMGFjYTJiYTQ5YWQ3NjQ2NzM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T22:15:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T22:15:02Z"
      },
      "message": "perf(app): the program-ahead digest reads a path signature stored at the write\n\n#153 review B1: since #109 every unposed op's stamp digests the ops\nahead, and the digest cloned and hashed each predecessor's whole\ntoolpath - inside status_of, which the status bar and the browser ask\nfor every op every frame (M^2 path clones per frame).\n\nschema::Toolpath now carries a private signature (path_sig::of, the old\nrest::path_hash) computed in Toolpath::new, its only constructor; the\ndigest and the stale story read it through a borrowed component and\nclone nothing. Only the prior plan and the pilot credit, which cut the\ngrid, still copy moves.\n\nReview N3: the predecessor's kind tag joins the digest (the prior plan\nand the pilot credit branch on it). N1: a Regenerate All round defers\nan op that reads the program ahead when an op ahead of it in its setup\nis staged in that round, so each op generates once.\n\nPinned by the_program_ahead_digest_moves_only_with_the_path,\na_reorder_marks_the_dependent_stale and\na_posed_op_keeps_its_stamp_when_the_program_ahead_moves\n(vertical_rapid_stock).\n\nRefs #109\nRefs #145\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
