      },
      "message": "fix(app): a refused op ahead no longer holds back the ops Regenerate All deferred behind it\n\n#153 re-review: the rounds loop stopped on a round with no successful\nresults, so when an op ahead staged and its generator refused, every\ndependent deferred behind it in that round was never regenerated and\nwas misreported as \"still stale after N round(s)\".\n\nThe loop now stops only when a round staged nothing. A refusal is final\n(the op is in `skipped` and excluded from later rounds), so the ops it\nheld back run next round against the world as it stands. The leftover\nmessage counts the rounds actually run.\n\nPinned by a_refused_op_ahead_does_not_hold_back_the_ops_behind_it\n(vertical_rapid_stock): a staged face whose clearance the grown stock\novertops refuses by name; the contour behind it is regenerated and\njudged, and is the only op regenerated.\n\nRefs #145\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
